# Disclosure

> Lede 0.7.2's docs for Disclosure, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/disclosure.md

A `<section>` whose heading opens and closes its body, with a summary that reads while it's closed. Built on Base UI Collapsible.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/disclosure
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md) and [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md), and the npm packages `@base-ui/react@^1.9.0`. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.2/disclosure.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { Disclosure } from '@/components/lede/disclosure';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/disclosure.tsx` | `@/components/lede/disclosure` | `Disclosure` (component), `DisclosureProps` (type) |

## Props

Base UI Collapsible: a `<section>`, a heading holding a `<button aria-expanded>` and a panel kept in the DOM as `hidden="until-found"`, so find-in-page can reveal it. Other HTML attributes and `ref` go on the `<section>`, so an `id` makes the whole level a deep-link target: a link to it scrolls to the level and leaves it closed.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  | The level's name. |
| `summary` | `React.ReactNode` |  | The takeaway: enough to decide or act without opening. Every Disclosure should have one. |
| `meta` | `React.ReactNode` |  | A short trailing figure: a count, a total, a status word. |
| `open` | `boolean` |  |  |
| `defaultOpen` | `boolean` |  |  |
| `onOpenChange` | `(open: boolean) => void` |  |  |
| `variant` | `'card' \| 'plain'` | `card` | `'card'` is a card of its own, and `'plain'` is separated by hairlines, for nesting inside a Card. Default `'card'`. |
| `headingLevel` | `2 \| 3 \| 4 \| 5 \| 6` | `3` | Level of the real heading the trigger sits in. Default 3. |
| `children` | `React.ReactNode` |  | The next level down. |

Disclosure also takes the attributes of `<section>`, such as `className`.

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { Disclosure } from '@/components/lede/disclosure';

export function WeekSummary() {
  return (
    <Disclosure title="This week" summary="2 decisions need you by Thursday" meta="2">
      <p>The budget review and the launch date.</p>
    </Disclosure>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

